- net

' The foot at /io/mesa: the one place a world meets Mesa. It holds the world's
' engine and its signing key, which are never records, and it keeps nothing a
' restart cannot rebuild. What it serves is derived from the world's own
' history the first time it is asked for; what it holds of other worlds is
' their mounts and the cards beside them. These are its rules, as steps over
' its own state and the world's state. The actor that owns the socket runs
' them and admits what they ask to have landed.
'
' Pages are named publ/<kind>|<audience>|<x>|<y>. The audience is the number
' of the world a root is published to, or 0 for the public root.
'   e|aud|base|head   an epic of that root from version base (0: from
'                     nothing) to version head, without its records
'   p|aud|head|hash   the pin with that hash, shown in the epic at head
'   h|aud|0|head      not a page: the name a hint carries, where a root stands
' A version is a stamp (net/stamp), so a name means one content for ever and
' a page never changes once bound.
+ mesa_foot
  + limits
    ' Packet, name and fragment sizes: Mesa's defaults.
    ^ row[nat]
    [1472 256 1024]
  + most
    ' The most streams one epic may make a reader fetch, and the most bytes.
    ^ nat
    65536
  + room
    ^ nat
    268435456
  + page
    ' The most bytes Mesa carries as one page.
    ^ nat
    1048576
  + peer
    ' A world this one corresponds with: its name, the number Mesa knows it
    ' by, and the key it signs with.
    : world=iota id=nat key=nat
  + ask
    ' A page asked for and not yet answered: of whom, and its name's parts.
    : request=nat from=nat kind=nat aud=nat a=nat b=nat
  + stream
    ' A pin's bytes as they arrived, checked against the hash that named them.
    : hash=nat bytes=nat
  + load
    ' An epic of one publisher's root being gathered: the streams that have
    ' arrived for it, the hashes asked for and not yet answered, and those
    ' still to ask for. Only a window of them is asked for at once.
    : from=nat aud=nat epic=net/epic streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] wanted=row[nat] queued=row[nat] size=nat
  + window
    ' The most pages of one epic asked for at once.
    ^ nat
    16
  + shown
    ' A pin this world has shown to an audience in an epic it served.
    : bytes=nat
  + landing
    ' A landing the world has been asked to admit.
    : request=nat from=nat aud=nat head=nat
  + effect
    ' What the foot asks of the actor that runs it.
    & mesa_foot/effect/send
      mesa_foot/effect/admit
    + send
      : to=nat packet=nat
    + admit
      : request=nat plan={\ namespace}either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
  + foot
    : self=iota seed=nat rift=nat engine=nat peers=row[mesa_foot/peer] next=nat
      asks=row[mesa_foot/ask] loads=row[mesa_foot/load]
      lands=row[mesa_foot/landing]
      bound=mop[path nat lt_pith] shown=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      told=mop[path nat lt_pith]
  + turn
    ' What a step leaves: the foot, and what it asks to have done.
    : foot=mesa_foot/foot does=row[mesa_foot/effect]
  + id
    ' The number Mesa knows a world by.
    \ world=iota
    ^ nat
    | quip_val world
  + start
    ' A foot for a world. Its engine knows each peer's key; the set is fixed
    ' for the engine's life, so a new peer means a new foot, which costs
    ' nothing: an engine holds nothing durable.
    \ self=iota seed=nat rift=nat peers=row[mesa_foot/peer]
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    = others=row[row[nat]]
        | peers.map
          \ item=mesa_foot/peer
          ^ row[nat]
          [item.id item.key]
      ;engine (MesaEngine (mesa_foot/id self) seed mesa_foot/limits others)
      asks=row[mesa_foot/ask] []
      loads=row[mesa_foot/load] []
      lands=row[mesa_foot/landing] []
      bound=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      shown=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      told=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
    | mesa_foot/foot self seed rift engine peers 1 asks loads lands bound shown told
  + renew
    ' The same foot with a new engine: when the engine's budget for bound
    ' pages is spent. Bound pages are derived again when next asked for;
    ' reads in flight are dropped, and a later hint starts them again.
    \ foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    = fresh (mesa_foot/start foot.self foot.seed foot.rift foot.peers)
    | fresh.set_next(foot.next).set_lands(foot.lands).set_shown(foot.shown).set_told(foot.told)
  + quiet
    \ foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = none=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
    | mesa_foot/turn foot none
  + peer_of
    \ id=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[mesa_foot/peer]
    = none=maybe[mesa_foot/peer] .none
      found foot.peers.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/peer (eq item.id id)))
    ? !(found.len) none
    | ./some found.at(0)
  + link
    ' The number Mesa knows a peer's link by: its place among the peers.
    \ id=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    % i=nat 0
    ^ nat
    ? (ge i foot.peers.len) 0
    ? (eq foot.peers.at(i).id id) i.inc
    | _ i.inc
  + mine
    ' The root this world publishes to an audience.
    \ aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
      public=path [foot.self 'our 'public]
    ? (eq aud 0) (./some public)
    ?> (./some item) (mesa_foot/peer_of aud foot) none
    = pairwise=path [foot.self 'our item.world]
    | ./some pairwise
  + theirs
    ' A publisher's root as it spells it: the one for this world, or its
    ' public one.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ path
    = open=path [from.world 'our 'public]
      pairwise=path [from.world 'our foot.self]
    ? public open
    pairwise
  + mount
    ' Where this world holds a publisher's root.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ path
    = root (mesa_foot/theirs from public foot)
    | (reference_index/mounted foot.self root).fall(root)
  + card
    ' Where this world keeps how such a mount stands.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ path
    = pairwise=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa from.world]
      open=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa from.world 'public]
    ? public open
    pairwise
  + head
    ' Where a root this world publishes stands; 0 while it holds nothing.
    \ root=path state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    = case state.case(.z root).fall(0)
    ? (eq 0 case) 0
    | net/stamp foot.rift case
  + sends
    ' What an engine asks to have sent.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]]
    ^ row[mesa_foot/effect]
    = none=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
    | acts.fold none
      \ out=row[mesa_foot/effect] act=row[nat]
      ^ row[mesa_foot/effect]
      ? !(eq 1 act.at(0)) out
      | out.snoc((mesa_foot/effect/send act.at(1) act.at(3)))
  + after
    ' One turn and then another, as one.
    \ first=mesa_foot/turn next={\ mesa_foot/foot}mesa_foot/turn
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = second (next first.foot)
    | mesa_foot/turn second.foot first.does.weld(second.does)
  + epic
    ' The change of a root between two of its versions, when this world can
    ' state it exactly: both of this continuity, and both in its history.
    \ root=path base=nat head=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[net/epic]
    = w32 4294967296
      none=maybe[net/epic] .none
    ? !(eq (div head w32) foot.rift) none
    ? !((eq base 0) || (eq (div base w32) foot.rift)) none
    | net/delta foot.rift root (mod base w32) (mod head w32) state
  + spot
    \ aud=nat hash=nat
    ^ path
    [($u aud) ($u hash)]
  + parts
    ' A pin and every pin beneath it, each by its hash, as shown to an
    ' audience.
    \ aud=nat top=pin[any] out=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    = at (mesa_foot/spot aud (PinHash top))
    ? out.has(at) out
    = kept out.put(at (mesa_foot/shown (PinBytes top)))
      inner=row[pin[any]] (PinParts top)
    | inner.fold kept
      \ acc=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] part=pin[any]
      ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      | mesa_foot/parts aud part acc
  + show
    ' Remember what an epic shows its audience: each record it names, and
    ' the pins those hold. A cache: what is missing from it is derived again
    ' from the head a name carries.
    \ aud=nat epic=net/epic out=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    = fresh=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      room (? (gt out.size 16384) fresh out)
    | epic.entries.fold room
      \ acc=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] item=net/entry
      ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      ?> (./some record) item.record acc
      = held=pin[any] (pin record)
      | mesa_foot/parts aud held acc
  + served
    : foot=mesa_foot/foot acts=row[row[nat]]
  + serve
    ' Bind the page a name asks for, the first time it is asked for, when
    ' it is one this world can answer.
    \ name=row[nat] spelled=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/served
    = none=row[row[nat]] []
      idle (mesa_foot/served foot none)
      key=path [($u spelled)]
    ? foot.bound.has(key) idle
    = kind name.at(0)
      aud name.at(1)
    ?> (./some root) (mesa_foot/mine aud foot) idle
    ? (eq kind 101)
      ?> (./some change) (mesa_foot/epic root name.at(2) name.at(3) state foot) idle
      = sealed (net/seal foot.seed root change)
        sent=[base=nat head=nat sig=nat lines=row[[rel=path stamp=nat sig=nat hash=nat]]] (net/wired sealed)
        page (PinBytes (pin sent))
        shown (mesa_foot/show aud sealed foot.shown)
      | mesa_foot/bind key spelled page foot.set_shown(shown)
    ? !(eq kind 112) idle
    = at (mesa_foot/spot aud name.at(3))
      known
        ? foot.shown.has(at) foot.shown
        ?> (./some all) (mesa_foot/epic root 0 name.at(2) state foot) foot.shown
        | mesa_foot/show aud all foot.shown
    ?> (./some item) known.get(at) (mesa_foot/served foot.set_shown(known) none)
    | mesa_foot/bind key spelled item.bytes foot.set_shown(known)
  + refused_call
    ' Whether the engine refused a call outright.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]]
    ^ bool
    | acts.any((\ act=row[nat] (eq 5 act.at(0))))
  + bind
    ' Bind a page under its name. A page over Mesa's size for one is not
    ' served at all: a value that large crosses as pins. An engine that has
    ' no room left is replaced by a new one, once.
    \ key=path spelled=nat page=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/served
    = none=row[row[nat]] []
    ? (gt (wid page) (inc mesa_foot/page)) (mesa_foot/served foot none)
    = ;acts (MesaBind foot.engine spelled page)
    ? !(mesa_foot/refused_call acts) (mesa_foot/served foot.set_bound(foot.bound.put(key 1)) acts)
    = again (mesa_foot/renew foot)
      ;second (MesaBind again.engine spelled page)
    ? (mesa_foot/refused_call second) (mesa_foot/served again none)
    | mesa_foot/served again.set_bound(again.bound.put(key 1)) second
  + read_page
    ' Ask a peer for a page.
    \ from=nat kind=nat aud=nat a=nat b=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = request foot.next
      ;acts (MesaRead foot.engine request from (MesaName kind aud a b))
      asked foot.set_next(request.inc).set_asks(foot.asks.snoc((mesa_foot/ask request from kind aud a b)))
    ? (mesa_foot/refused_call acts) (mesa_foot/finished request 1 0 state asked)
    | mesa_foot/acted acts state asked
  + acted
    ' Do what an engine asks: send what it sends, and take up each read
    ' that finished.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = sent (mesa_foot/turn foot (mesa_foot/sends acts))
    | acts.fold sent
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn act=row[nat]
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      ? !(eq 2 act.at(0)) acc
      | mesa_foot/after acc
        \ now=mesa_foot/foot
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        | mesa_foot/finished act.at(1) act.at(2) act.at(3) state now
  + hint
    ' Tell a peer where the root published to it stands, and what this
    ' world holds of the same root of its own. A hint carries no data and
    ' is not believed: its receiver compares and then reads.
    \ to=mesa_foot/peer public=bool state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/effect
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      root=path (? public [foot.self 'our 'public] [foot.self 'our to.world])
      offered (mesa_foot/head root state foot)
      held (net/held ['head] (mesa_foot/card to public foot) state)
      holds (MesaName 104 (? public 0 me) 0 held)
      offers (MesaName 104 (? public 0 to.id) 0 offered)
    | mesa_foot/effect/send to.id (MesaHint me to.id holds offers mesa_foot/limits)
  + mark
    ' What a hint to a peer said, as one number.
    \ to=mesa_foot/peer public=bool state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    = root=path (? public [foot.self 'our 'public] [foot.self 'our to.world])
      offered (mesa_foot/head root state foot)
      held (net/held ['head] (mesa_foot/card to public foot) state)
    | add (mul offered 18446744073709551616) held
  + turned
    ' The world committed: hint each peer whose roots, or what is held of
    ' its roots, moved since it was last told.
    \ state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = both=row[bool] [.false .true]
    | foot.peers.fold (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn item=mesa_foot/peer
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      | both.fold acc
        \ had=mesa_foot/turn public=bool
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        = at=path [($u item.id) ($u (? public 1 0))]
          now (mesa_foot/mark item public state had.foot)
        ? (eq now had.foot.told.get(at).fall(0)) had
        | mesa_foot/turn had.foot.set_told(had.foot.told.put(at now)) had.does.snoc((mesa_foot/hint item public state had.foot))
  + clock
    ' Time passed: let the engine retry or give up what it has in flight.
    \ now=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = ;acts (MesaAdvance foot.engine now)
    | mesa_foot/acted acts state foot
  + tick
    ' Time passed, and it is time to say again where things stand: tell
    ' every peer, so a lost hint is repaired.
    \ now=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = moved (mesa_foot/clock now state foot)
      hints
        | moved.foot.peers.fold moved.does
          \ out=row[mesa_foot/effect] item=mesa_foot/peer
          ^ row[mesa_foot/effect]
          | out.snoc((mesa_foot/hint item .false state moved.foot)).snoc((mesa_foot/hint item .true state moved.foot))
    | mesa_foot/turn moved.foot hints
  + busy
    ' Whether something of a publisher's root is already on its way.
    \ from=nat aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ bool
    ? (foot.asks.any((\ item=mesa_foot/ask (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))) .true
    ? (foot.loads.any((\ item=mesa_foot/load (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))) .true
    | foot.lands.any((\ item=mesa_foot/landing (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))
  + hinted
    ' A peer said where its root for this world stands and what it holds of
    ' this world's. Read the first when it is past what is held and was not
    ' refused; answer the second with a hint when the peer is behind.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer holds=nat offers=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      offered (MesaParse offers)
      held (MesaParse holds)
      sought
        ? !(eq offered.len 4) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        ? !(eq offered.at(0) 104) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        = aud offered.at(1)
          public (eq aud 0)
        ? !((eq aud 0) || (eq aud me)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        = card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
        ? !(net/wants card offered.at(3) state) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        ? (mesa_foot/busy from.id aud foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 101 aud (net/held ['head] card state) offered.at(3) state foot
    ? !(eq held.len 4) sought
    ? !(eq held.at(0) 104) sought
    = aud held.at(1)
      public (eq aud 0)
    ? !((eq aud 0) || (eq aud from.id)) sought
    ?> (./some root) (mesa_foot/mine aud sought.foot) sought
    ? !(gt (mesa_foot/head root state sought.foot) held.at(3)) sought
    | mesa_foot/turn sought.foot sought.does.snoc((mesa_foot/hint from public state sought.foot))
  + heard
    ' A packet arrived from a peer. A hint is compared. An ask is let
    ' through only for a name this world serves to that peer: the public
    ' root, or the root published to it. Anything else is the engine's.
    \ from=nat packet=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of from foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = seen (MesaLook packet mesa_foot/limits)
      kind seen.at(0)
    ? (eq kind 9) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? (eq kind 2) (mesa_foot/hinted sender seen.at(1) seen.at(2) state foot)
    ? !(eq kind 0) (mesa_foot/receive from packet mesa_foot/none state foot)
    = name (MesaParse seen.at(1))
    ? !(eq name.len 4) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? !((eq name.at(1) 0) || (eq name.at(1) from)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = ready (mesa_foot/serve name seen.at(1) state foot)
    | mesa_foot/receive from packet ready.acts state ready.foot
  + none
    ^ row[row[nat]]
    []
  + receive
    \ from=nat packet=nat before=row[row[nat]] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = ;acts (MesaReceive foot.engine from (mesa_foot/link from foot) packet)
    | mesa_foot/acted before.weld(acts) state foot
  + finished
    ' A read ended: with its page, or without.
    \ request=nat status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = found foot.asks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/ask (eq item.request request)))
    ? !(found.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = asked found.at(0)
      cleared foot.set_asks(foot.asks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/ask !(eq item.request request))))
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of asked.from cleared) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq asked.kind 101) (mesa_foot/got_epic sender asked status bytes state cleared)
    | mesa_foot/got_pin sender asked status bytes state cleared
  + refused
    ' Note on the mount's card that a head was refused and why, so it is
    ' not asked for again.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool head=nat why=iota foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
      plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        | either/ok[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]] (net/refuse card head why now)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + got_epic
    ' An epic arrived, without its records. Nothing is assumed of it: it
    ' must be an epic, the one asked for, and its publisher's. Then each
    ' record this world lacks is asked for by its hash. A publisher that
    ' cannot state the change from where this world stands sends nothing,
    ' and is asked for everything.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq asked.aud 0)
      idle (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? !(eq status 0)
      ? (eq asked.a 0) idle
      | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 101 asked.aud 0 asked.b state foot
    = stored=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    ?> (./some held) stored idle
    ?> (./some change) (net/read (unpin held)) idle
    ? !(and (eq change.base asked.a) (eq change.head asked.b)) idle
    = mount (mesa_foot/mount from public foot)
      card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
      root (mesa_foot/theirs from public foot)
    ? !(net/proven (net/key card state) root change) (mesa_foot/refused from public change.head 'net_forged foot)
    = lacking (net/lacks mount change state)
      streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] []
      nothing=row[nat] []
      fresh (mesa_foot/load from.id asked.aud change streams nothing lacking 0)
    | mesa_foot/pump from fresh state foot
  + without
    ' The loads other than one publisher root's.
    \ from=nat aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    | foot.set_loads(foot.loads.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/load !(and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud)))))
  + got_pin
    ' A pin's bytes arrived. They must hash to the name they were asked by.
    ' Each pin they name is asked for in turn, and when none is left the
    ' epic is complete. When a page never comes this epic is given up; a
    ' later hint starts again.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq asked.aud 0)
      held foot.loads.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/load (and (and (eq item.from asked.from) (eq item.aud asked.aud)) (eq item.epic.head asked.a))))
    ? !(held.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = gathering held.at(0)
      rest (mesa_foot/without asked.from asked.aud foot)
    ? !(eq status 0) (mesa_foot/quiet rest)
    ? !(eq (Sha256 bytes) asked.b) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit rest)
    = streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] gathering.streams.snoc((mesa_foot/stream asked.b bytes))
      size (add gathering.size (wid bytes))
    ? (gt streams.len mesa_foot/most) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit rest)
    ? (gt size mesa_foot/room) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit rest)
    = still=row[nat] gathering.wanted.keep((\ hash=nat !(eq hash asked.b)))
      named=row[nat] (PinNames bytes)
      more=row[nat]
        | named.keep
          \ hash=nat
          ^ bool
          ? (streams.any((\ item=mesa_foot/stream (eq item.hash hash)))) .false
          ? (still.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen hash)))) .false
          ? (gathering.queued.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen hash)))) .false
          .true
      next gathering.set_streams(streams).set_wanted(still).set_queued(gathering.queued.weld(more)).set_size(size)
    | mesa_foot/pump from next state rest
  + pump
    ' Ask for more of an epic's pages, up to the window; when none is asked
    ' for and none is left to ask for, the epic is complete. The foot given
    ' is one that does not hold this load; the one answered holds it as it
    ' now stands.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer gathering=mesa_foot/load state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = room (? (lt gathering.wanted.len mesa_foot/window) (sub mesa_foot/window gathering.wanted.len) 0)
      count (? (lt gathering.queued.len room) gathering.queued.len room)
      asking=row[nat] gathering.queued.take(count)
      next gathering.set_wanted(gathering.wanted.weld(asking)).set_queued(gathering.queued.drop(count))
      loading foot.set_loads(foot.loads.snoc(next))
    ? (and (eq 0 next.wanted.len) (eq 0 next.queued.len)) (mesa_foot/complete from next state loading)
    | asking.fold (mesa_foot/quiet loading)
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn hash=nat
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      | mesa_foot/after acc
        \ now=mesa_foot/foot
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 112 gathering.aud gathering.epic.head hash state now
  + staged
    ' Whether a stream loads into the store now: it does once every pin it
    ' names has, and never when it holds code.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ bool
    = found=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    | maybe/is_some found
  + rebuild
    ' Load every stream, a pin's parts before the pin. Parts arrive after
    ' what names them, so the last to arrive go first; whatever a pass
    ' leaves is tried again while passes still load something.
    \ streams=row[mesa_foot/stream]
    ^ bool
    % left=row[mesa_foot/stream] streams.rev
    ^ bool
    ? !(left.len) .true
    = ;after (left.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/stream !(mesa_foot/staged item.bytes))))
    ? (eq after.len left.len) .false
    | _ after
  + record
    ' The record a stream holds, when it is one.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ maybe[myth]
    = none=maybe[myth] .none
      found=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    ?> (./some held) found none
    | net/sound (unpin held)
  + plan
    ' Land an epic. When the rules refuse it for what it is, rather than
    ' for when it came, note that on the card instead.
    \ mount=path card=path change=net/epic now=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    ? (net/land mount card change now)
     > (./ok writes) (either/ok[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]] writes)
     > (./err why)
      ? (eq_iota why 'net_stale) (./err why)
      ? (eq_iota why 'net_gap) (./err why)
      | either/ok[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]] (net/refuse card change.head why now)
  + complete
    ' Every stream of an epic has arrived: rebuild its pins, put each
    ' record where its hash is named, and ask the world to land it as one
    ' event.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer gathered=mesa_foot/load state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq gathered.aud 0)
      rest (mesa_foot/without gathered.from gathered.aud foot)
      head gathered.epic.head
      ;whole (mesa_foot/rebuild gathered.streams)
    ? !whole (mesa_foot/refused from public head 'net_unfit rest)
    = start=maybe[net/epic] (./some gathered.epic)
      none=maybe[net/epic] .none
      filled
        | gathered.epic.entries.fold start
          \ acc=maybe[net/epic] item=net/entry
          ^ maybe[net/epic]
          ?> (./some change) acc none
          ? (eq 0 item.hash) acc
          = found gathered.streams.keep((\ got=mesa_foot/stream (eq got.hash item.hash)))
          ? !(found.len) acc
          ?> (./some record) (mesa_foot/record found.at(0).bytes) none
          | ./some (net/given item.hash record change)
    ?> (./some change) filled (mesa_foot/refused from public head 'net_unfit rest)
    = mount (mesa_foot/mount from public foot)
      card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
      request rest.next
      plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        | mesa_foot/plan mount card change now
      waiting rest.set_next(request.inc).set_lands(rest.lands.snoc((mesa_foot/landing request gathered.from gathered.aud head)))
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit request plan)]
    | mesa_foot/turn waiting does
  + landed
    ' The world answered a landing. One the kernel refused, a record that
    ' breaks its own contract say, is noted on the card with the reason.
    \ request=nat why=maybe[iota] foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = found foot.lands.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/landing (eq item.request request)))
    ? !(found.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = was found.at(0)
      cleared foot.set_lands(foot.lands.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/landing !(eq item.request request))))
    ?> (./some reason) why (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq_iota reason 'net_stale) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq_iota reason 'net_gap) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of was.from cleared) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    | mesa_foot/refused sender (eq was.aud 0) was.head reason cleared
